an  applauded  young leaders and their advocacy and  encouraged them to keep fighting  i say to you keep challenging  keep pushing make them a little  uncomfortable because it's only in that  discomfort that we actually create the  conditions  to reimagine our standards our policies  and our leadership to move towards real  representation  and meaningful influence over the  structures of decision-making  and power and the former actress had  this to say about  overcoming fear and often it's fear that  paralyzes us and stops us from being  brave  but don't underestimate that you have  some of those answers within  don't underestimate your  in addition to emphasizing the need to  trust your gut  megan revealed her biggest struggle  throughout her advocacy work  the hardest part and it was the hardest  part for me  is to chase your convictions with action  the growth and the change that you're  pursuing might not feel like anything  day to day  but when you look back i promise you  will see that it all  adds and just in case you need a little  help along the way  i will be cheering you on so will my  husband so will archie  as you all continue marching advocating  and leading the way forward prior to her  speech a source close to the duchess  told e.t  why she's so passionate about advocating  for women  quote the duchess strongly believes that  the next generation of girls and  young women have incredible power and  have already shown themselves to be  leaders beyond their years  they are a generation that is  challenging norms enacting real world  change  and leading global movements what's more  the source adds that megan doesn't just  believe the next generation  is not only poised to change the world  megan thinks they've already begun  last month the former actress delivered  a similar inspired message to the  graduating class of her alma mater  immaculate heart the only wrong thing to  say  is to say nothing
 

